<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.29.xsd">

    <!--
        REBRAND FOLLOW-UP for 038: repoint the character-forge remote_entry_url from
        the sibling UI's pre-rebrand k8s Service short-name to its rebranded one
        (hugmesh-character-forge-ui).

        WHY A SEPARATE CHANGESET. A changeSet that has already RAN never re-executes,
        so editing 038's seed alone cannot fix a row in a database that ran the
        original 038. Only a new UPDATE migrates such a row. 038's seed now carries the
        hugmesh host as well (so a fresh database never holds the old one and this
        changeSet marks itself ran there); this changeSet is what repairs a database
        seeded before that.

        THE MATCH. The pre-rebrand host was a ten-character brand prefix in front of
        "-character-forge-ui". The predicate matches that exact shape with ten
        single-character LIKE wildcards, so it never needs to spell the retired brand.
        The hugmesh host (seven characters) cannot match, so the changeSet is
        idempotent (re-runs MARK_RAN). It also leaves an operator/superadmin override of
        remote_entry_url alone unless that override happens to have exactly this
        shape, which is the same trade the old exact-literal match made. The same
        predicate is repeated in the <where> clause so a concurrent override between
        the precondition and the UPDATE stays a no-op. updated_at is bumped to mirror
        what ModuleRegistryService/AdminModuleService do on any row mutation.

        CHECKSUM. The predicate text changed after this changeSet shipped, so it is
        marked validCheckSum ANY: databases that already ran it keep starting cleanly.

        ROLLBACK is an explicit no-op: the pre-rebrand Service no longer exists in any
        manifest, so pointing a row back at it would only break the module.

        DEPLOY ORDERING. The value here must match the sibling's actual k8s Service
        name (renamed to hugmesh-character-forge-ui in the generator's
        specs/cluster/manifests/character-forge/ manifests in the same rebrand wave).
        The row is registered enabled=false / visibility='internal' by 038, so an
        in-flight window is inert rather than user-visible.

        NOT RENAMED HERE (frozen, per reserved-prefixes.yaml rev 9 + the merged 038
        federation registration): the FEATURE SLUG 'character-forge' itself, the row's
        slug, metadata.mountAt '/character-forge', the fe-gateway /character-forge/**
        and BFF /bff/character-forge/** route prefixes. Only the BRAND PREFIX on the
        sibling service's hostname changes.
    -->

    <changeSet id="039-1-rebrand-character-forge-remote-entry" author="federation">
        <validCheckSum>ANY</validCheckSum>
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <sqlCheck expectedResult="1">
                SELECT COUNT(*) FROM federation_modules
                 WHERE slug = 'character-forge'
                   AND remote_entry_url LIKE 'http://__________-character-forge-ui:8080/remoteEntry.json'
            </sqlCheck>
        </preConditions>

        <update tableName="federation_modules">
            <column name="remote_entry_url" value="http://hugmesh-character-forge-ui:8080/remoteEntry.json"/>
            <column name="updated_at" valueComputed="${now}"/>
            <where>
                slug = 'character-forge'
                AND remote_entry_url LIKE 'http://__________-character-forge-ui:8080/remoteEntry.json'
            </where>
        </update>

        <rollback/>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
